1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,160
Anyone can make a certificate look real.

2
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:05,727
A PDF can be edited.

3
00:00:05,727 --> 00:00:07,528
A screenshot can be faked.

4
00:00:07,528 --> 00:00:09,440
A link can be quietly swapped.

5
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:12,137
So when someone hands you a credential,

6
00:00:12,137 --> 00:00:13,820
what are you actually trusting?

7
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:15,900
This is Credentia.

8
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:19,638
An issuer anchors a fingerprint of the credential on Monad.

9
00:00:19,638 --> 00:00:22,020
Anyone with the link can check it themselves.

10
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:25,288
Here's a real credential on Monad testnet.

11
00:00:25,288 --> 00:00:26,911
The registry confirms it.

12
00:00:26,911 --> 00:00:29,200
The details match, and it's still active.

13
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:33,410
Now watch what happens if one detail in the link is changed.

14
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:36,233
The fingerprint no longer matches.

15
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:38,330
Credentia says so, plainly.

16
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,401
And when an issuer withdraws a credential, the page shows it.

17
00:00:42,401 --> 00:00:43,940
Revoked, on chain.

18
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:47,996
Behind the page, an Envio indexer, running locally,

19
00:00:47,996 --> 00:00:50,457
turns raw chain events into a timeline.

20
00:00:50,457 --> 00:00:52,030
Issued, then revoked.

21
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:58,760
These are real transactions on Monad testnet, backed by 178 contract tests

22
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,340
and 242 web tests.

23
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:03,580
And the flow has been backtested with five people.

24
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:05,643
It's a testnet demo.

25
00:01:05,643 --> 00:01:08,780
The data is labelled, and the identity gate is a stand-in.

26
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:10,766
Credentia.

27
00:01:10,766 --> 00:01:12,326
Don't trust the claim.

28
00:01:12,326 --> 00:01:13,690
Verify the credential.
